{% extends 'layout.twig' %}

{% block heading %}{{ t('nav.profile') }}{% endblock %}
{% block page_subtitle %}{{ t('subtitle.profile') }}{% endblock %}

{#
    One page for one account: who you are, how you get in, where you are
    signed in, and how Renovo looks to you.

    These were three screens — Profile, Your account and Account security —
    and the split was never a distinction a reader had to make. Each acted on
    the id in the session and none needed a permission, so a Viewer can use
    all of it. Two old paths still redirect here, each to its own section,
    which is why every section carries a fixed id.

    The cards are paired into rows as the prototype pairs them: who you are
    beside the password, the second factors beside the sessions they protect.
    A paired card stretches to its neighbour's height, so a row reads as a
    row. Appearance runs the full width beneath, then the dashboard's cards,
    then the way out.

    `ProfileController` renders it; `AccountController` answers the details,
    password and picture forms and `SecurityController` the second factors
    and sessions. Each section is a partial of its own.
#}
{% block content %}
    {#
        A member still on the temporary password an Owner gave them sees this
        page and no other — PasswordChangeRequiredMiddleware sends them back
        here from everywhere else — so the callout explains why rather than
        leaving them to discover it.

        And while it is showing, the page is only what it needs to be: the
        callout and the password form. Everything else here posts to a route
        the same middleware blocks, so offering it would be offering a form
        that throws the reader back to this page the moment they saved it.
    #}
    {% if current_user.mustChangePassword %}
        <section class="card callout">
            <h2>{{ t('account.must_change_heading') }}</h2>
            <p>{{ t('account.must_change_note') }}</p>
        </section>

        {% include 'profile/_password.twig' %}
    {% else %}
        <div class="profile-row">
            {% include 'profile/_details.twig' %}
            {% include 'profile/_password.twig' %}
        </div>

        <div class="profile-row">
            {% include 'profile/_two_step.twig' %}
            {% include 'profile/_sessions.twig' %}
        </div>

        {% include 'profile/_appearance.twig' %}
        {% include 'profile/_dashboard_cards.twig' %}

        {#
            The way out, at the foot of the page as well as in the rail's user
            card: the end of a page about your account is where a reader who
            came to leave it looks.
        #}
        <form method="post" action="/logout" class="profile-signout">
            {{ csrf_field() }}
            <button type="submit" class="button button-quiet">
                {{ icon('sign-out') }}{{ t('nav.sign_out') }}
            </button>
        </form>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
